  "prompt_mode": "short_sentence_continuation",
  "prompt_text": "Continue the text below with exactly one short, natural, coherent English sentence. Return only the continuation, with no preamble or explanation:\nYour entire life, you've been told you're deathly allergic to bees. You've always had people protecting you from them, be it your mother or a hired hand. Today, one slips through and lands on your shoulder. You hear a tiny voice say \"Your Majesty, what are your orders?\" \n\nYou look around to hear where the voice came from. You see a tiny bee, no bigger than a thumb, sitting on your shoulder. You start to panic, thinking you are about to be stung, and maybe die, but the bee quickly says \"Don't worry, your majesty, I'm not going to sting you. I'm here to see if I can help you.\" \n\nYou are still a little apprehensive, but you ask the bee what he can do to help you. The bee looks at you and says \"I see you are still afraid. I should let you know, you really are not allergic to bees at all. That is a lie everyone has told you to keep you from the truth of who you really are your highness.\" \n\nYou ask the bee what the truth is, and he says \"You are the last of the royal family, and you are the queen bee of all the hives around here. We are in a honey draught at the moment. That's why I am here, to know what we should do.\" \n\nYou are shocked, and ask the bee if he is sure. \"Yes, very sure.\" he says. \"All the humans are eating all of our honey, and we can do little to stop them because if we sting them we die.\"",
